# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space for the latest version of Qiskit bosons"
msgstr "Sintesis gate Evolution dalam ruang boson untuk versi terkini Qiskit bosons"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space"
msgstr "Sintesis gate Evolution dalam ruang boson"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bosonic-synthesis-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space {#synthesize-an-evolution-gate-in-bosonic-space}"
msgstr "Sintesis gate Evolution dalam ruang boson {#synthesize-an-evolution-gate-in-bosonic-space}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The time evolution $e^{-itH}$ of a Hamiltonian that is a sum of non-commuting pieces cannot be implemented exactly gate by gate. A **product formula** approximates it by a sequence of short evolutions under the individual pieces, and the approximation error is called the Trotter error.\n"
msgstr "Evolusi masa $e^{-itH}$ bagi Hamiltonian yang merupakan hasil tambah bahagian yang tidak berkomutasi tidak dapat dilaksanakan dengan tepat gate demi gate. **Formula hasil darab** menganggarkannya dengan jujukan evolusi pendek di bawah setiap bahagian, dan ralat penganggaran itu dipanggil ralat Trotter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can apply a product formula in two places, and they are not interchangeable:\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh menggunakan formula hasil darab di dua tempat, dan keduanya tidak boleh ditukar ganti:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**In bosonic space**, before any truncation or encoding has been chosen. The formula sees the *groups* of the operator (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)) and can interleave them.\n"
msgstr "**Dalam ruang boson**, sebelum sebarang pemotongan atau pengekodan dipilih. Formula itu melihat *kumpulan* operator (lihat [Kumpulkan sebutan operator: gunakan struktur operator](grouping#grouping-explanation)) dan boleh menyelitkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**In qubit space**, inside Qiskit’s [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), after the operator has been mapped. The formula sees one Pauli operator per group and can only subdivide the terms *within* it.\n"
msgstr "**Dalam ruang qubit**, di dalam [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) Qiskit, selepas operator dipetakan. Formula itu melihat satu operator Pauli bagi setiap kumpulan dan hanya boleh membahagikan sebutan *di dalamnya*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only the first can reduce the error between groups that do not commute, which is usually the dominant one. This guide shows how to use it.\n"
msgstr "Hanya yang pertama dapat mengurangkan ralat antara kumpulan yang tidak berkomutasi, yang biasanya paling dominan. Panduan ini menunjukkan cara menggunakannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Both steps are optional. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate that is never decomposed in bosonic space reaches the boson-to-qubit stage whole and is mapped and synthesized there. That incurs *no* error at the bosonic level, only whatever the qubit-level formula introduces.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Kedua-dua langkah adalah pilihan. Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") yang tidak pernah diurai dalam ruang boson sampai ke peringkat boson-ke-qubit secara utuh dan dipetakan serta disintesis di situ. Itu *tidak* menimbulkan ralat pada peringkat boson, hanya apa sahaja yang diperkenalkan oleh formula peringkat qubit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up {#set-up}"
msgstr "Sediakan {#set-up}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A two-site Bose-Hubbard chain, the smallest example in which the groups do not commute (see [Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) for the full model). It is grouped into one Hermitian group for the bond and one diagonal group for the on-site interaction:\n"
msgstr "Rantai Bose-Hubbard dua tapak, contoh terkecil di mana kumpulan tidak berkomutasi (lihat [Simulasikan dinamik Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan pengekodan](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) untuk model penuh). Ia dikumpulkan menjadi satu kumpulan Hermitian untuk ikatan dan satu kumpulan pepenjuru untuk interaksi atas tapak:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To measure an error you need a reference. The exact evolution of the Hamiltonian *as mapped at the same truncation* is the right one, because the truncation is a separate approximation:\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengukur ralat anda memerlukan rujukan. Evolusi tepat bagi Hamiltonian *seperti yang dipetakan pada pemotongan yang sama* ialah yang betul, kerana pemotongan ialah penganggaran yang berasingan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `error` deliberately simulates the lowered circuit *without* decomposing its [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) instances. [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) applies each as the exact exponential of its group, so the only thing left is the product of group exponentials that the bosonic synthesis chose.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `error` sengaja mensimulasikan litar yang diturunkan *tanpa* mengurai instance [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)nya. [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) menggunakan setiap satu sebagai eksponen tepat bagi kumpulannya, jadi satu-satunya yang tinggal ialah hasil darab eksponen kumpulan yang dipilih oleh sintesis boson.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default {#the-default}"
msgstr "Lalai {#the-default}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With no `synthesis` argument an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate decomposes with [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\"), the first-order formula: one factor per group, each for the whole time.\n"
msgstr "Tanpa argumen `synthesis`, gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") diurai dengan [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\"), formula peringkat pertama: satu faktor bagi setiap kumpulan, masing-masing untuk keseluruhan masa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without decomposing, the whole gate is handed to the qubit stage and there is no bosonic Trotter error at all:\n"
msgstr "Tanpa penguraian, keseluruhan gate diserahkan kepada peringkat qubit dan tiada ralat Trotter boson sama sekali:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decomposed, a genuine error appears, because the two groups do not commute:\n"
msgstr "Apabila diurai, ralat sebenar muncul, kerana kedua-dua kumpulan tidak berkomutasi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reduce the error {#reduce-the-error}"
msgstr "Kurangkan ralat {#reduce-the-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass a different synthesis method to the gate. A higher **order** composes the factors symmetrically so that the leading error terms cancel; more **repetitions** divide the time into shorter steps.\n"
msgstr "Hantar kaedah sintesis yang berbeza kepada gate. **Tertib** yang lebih tinggi menyusun faktor secara simetri supaya sebutan ralat utama saling membatalkan; lebih banyak **ulangan** membahagikan masa kepada langkah yang lebih pendek.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each increase of the order by two composes five sweeps of the one below (the $5^{(k-2)/2}$ growth of Suzuki’s recursion, applied to the $2n - 1$ factors of order 2), which is the count in the last line, marked with a star. The sweeps meet on the same factor, so the neighboring gates evolve under one operator and are fused into a single gate with the summed time. That saves one gate per seam and is exact. Pass `merge_adjacent=False` to keep the textbook sequence. Either way, a higher order buys a smaller error:\n"
msgstr "Setiap peningkatan tertib sebanyak dua menyusun lima sapuan daripada tertib di bawahnya (pertumbuhan $5^{(k-2)/2}$ bagi rekursi Suzuki, diterapkan pada $2n - 1$ faktor tertib 2), iaitu bilangan pada baris terakhir, ditandakan dengan bintang. Sapuan itu bertemu pada faktor yang sama, jadi gate jiran berevolusi di bawah satu operator dan digabungkan menjadi satu gate dengan masa terjumlah. Itu menjimatkan satu gate bagi setiap sambungan dan adalah tepat. Hantar `merge_adjacent=False` untuk mengekalkan jujukan buku teks. Walau bagaimanapun, tertib yang lebih tinggi memberikan ralat yang lebih kecil:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repetitions trade depth for accuracy at a different rate. The first-order error falls linearly in the step size, the second-order one quadratically:\n"
msgstr "Ulangan menukar kedalaman dengan ketepatan pada kadar yang berbeza. Ralat peringkat pertama menurun secara linear mengikut saiz langkah, manakala peringkat kedua secara kuadratik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which is the better trade depends on the operator. Note that an operator with a single group is exact at any order, because a lone factor commutes with itself, and the formula then collapses to one gate rather than re-splitting it.\n"
msgstr "Yang mana pertukaran yang lebih baik bergantung pada operator. Perhatikan bahawa operator dengan satu kumpulan adalah tepat pada sebarang tertib, kerana faktor tunggal berkomutasi dengan dirinya sendiri, dan formula itu kemudian runtuh menjadi satu gate dan bukannya dipecahkan semula.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the cost {#measure-the-cost}"
msgstr "Ukur kos {#measure-the-cost}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A smaller error costs more factors, and each factor costs entangling gates once the qubit stage has synthesized it. How many depends on the encoding, so count them through the preset pipeline, with the basis fixed and no qubit-level optimization (`optimization_level=0`), to see the price of each method:\n"
msgstr "Ralat yang lebih kecil memerlukan lebih banyak faktor, dan setiap faktor memerlukan gate berbelit sebaik sahaja peringkat qubit mensintesisnya. Berapa banyak bergantung pada pengekodan, jadi kira melalui saluran paip pratetap, dengan asas ditetapkan dan tiada pengoptimuman peringkat qubit (`optimization_level=0`), untuk melihat harga setiap kaedah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The exact counts depend on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution gates, which changes between releases, so the plot shows them rather than a table:\n"
msgstr "Kiraan tepat bergantung pada cara Qiskit mensintesis gate evolusi, yang berubah antara keluaran, jadi plot menunjukkannya dan bukannya jadual:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Grouped bar chart of the CX count for Lie-Trotter and Suzuki of order 2 and 4, for the Gray and the unary encoding. The counts grow with the order, and the unary bars are higher.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bosonic_synthesis-10.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Grouped bar chart of the CX count for Lie-Trotter and Suzuki of order 2 and 4, for the Gray and the unary encoding. The counts grow with the order, and the unary bars are higher.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bosonic_synthesis-10.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each group of bars is a method: Lie-Trotter, Suzuki of order 2, and Suzuki of order 4. The order buys accuracy at a price that grows by the factor of the recursion, and the unary encoding pays more than the Gray code for every method because each of its factors maps to more entangling gates. Choose the method for the accuracy that you need and the encoding for the hardware, and keep the two choices apart: the bosonic circuit above never changes.\n"
msgstr "Setiap kumpulan bar ialah satu kaedah: Lie-Trotter, Suzuki tertib 2, dan Suzuki tertib 4. Tertib membeli ketepatan pada harga yang meningkat mengikut faktor rekursi, dan pengekodan unari membayar lebih daripada kod Gray bagi setiap kaedah kerana setiap faktornya dipetakan kepada lebih banyak gate berbelit. Pilih kaedah berdasarkan ketepatan yang anda perlukan dan pengekodan berdasarkan perkakasan, dan pisahkan kedua-dua pilihan itu: litar boson di atas tidak pernah berubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply one method to a whole circuit {#apply-one-method-to-a-whole-circuit}"
msgstr "Gunakan satu kaedah pada keseluruhan litar {#apply-one-method-to-a-whole-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To set `synthesis` on each gate, you must thread the choice through everything that builds one. The [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") pass makes the choice once for a pipeline instead. Its `config` names the method for each type of gate, and it both selects the method and expands the gates:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menetapkan `synthesis` pada setiap gate, anda mesti menyalurkan pilihan itu melalui segala yang membina satu. Pas [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") membuat pilihan itu sekali untuk satu saluran paip. `config`nya menamakan kaedah bagi setiap jenis gate, dan ia memilih kaedah serta mengembangkan gate:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A method can also be named, with the arguments for its `__init__`, instead of being built: `B2BSynthesis({\"Evolution\": (\"SuzukiTrotter\", (), {\"order\": 2})})`. The available names are those of the [`B2BSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-b-2-b-synthesis-plugin-manager#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager\"), and a method that is registered nowhere can be handed over as an instance, as above.\n"
msgstr "Kaedah juga boleh dinamakan, dengan argumen untuk `__init__`nya, dan bukannya dibina: `B2BSynthesis({\"Evolution\": (\"SuzukiTrotter\", (), {\"order\": 2})})`. Nama yang tersedia ialah nama dalam [`B2BSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-b-2-b-synthesis-plugin-manager#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.B2BSynthesisPluginManager\"), dan kaedah yang tidak didaftarkan di mana-mana boleh diserahkan sebagai instance, seperti di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `apply=False` the pass only selects the method and leaves the expansion to the point where it is wanted, for example to inspect the circuit first. An atomic gate is never touched, not even tagged:\n"
msgstr "Dengan `apply=False` pas itu hanya memilih kaedah dan membiarkan pengembangan sehingga ke titik yang dikehendaki, contohnya untuk memeriksa litar dahulu. Gate atomik tidak pernah disentuh, malah tidak ditanda:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An unexpanded gate reaches the boson-to-qubit stage whole, where it is mapped without its `synthesis` being consulted, so every method then produces identical output.\n"
msgstr "Gate yang tidak dikembangkan sampai ke peringkat boson-ke-qubit secara utuh, di mana ia dipetakan tanpa `synthesis`nya dirujuk, jadi setiap kaedah kemudian menghasilkan output yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An optional `filter` restricts it to the gates that benefit. Evolutions whose groups all commute, such as a Hamiltonian made only of number operators, are synthesized exactly at any order, so a higher order would only add depth there.\n"
msgstr "`filter` pilihan menghadkannya kepada gate yang mendapat manfaat. Evolusi yang semua kumpulannya berkomutasi, seperti Hamiltonian yang hanya terdiri daripada operator nombor, disintesis dengan tepat pada sebarang tertib, jadi tertib yang lebih tinggi hanya akan menambah kedalaman di situ.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restrict the pass to the gates that benefit {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"
msgstr "Hadkan pas kepada gate yang mendapat manfaat {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A purely diagonal operator makes the point concrete, because number operators commute with each other. Its groups are exact at first order, and the second order spends entangling gates for nothing:\n"
msgstr "Operator pepenjuru tulen menjelaskan perkara ini, kerana operator nombor berkomutasi sesama sendiri. Kumpulannya tepat pada peringkat pertama, dan peringkat kedua membelanjakan gate berbelit dengan sia-sia:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both circuits are exact, so the second spends more entangling gates for no gain. (The symmetric order-two formula applies the first group twice at half the time each, and thus the cost depends on which group comes first.) The `filter` takes a predicate over the [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) and leaves the rejected gates untouched, so one pass can raise the order on the gates that benefit and keep the rest at first order. The predicate below accepts a gate only when its operator moves bosons between modes, which is when the groups fail to commute:\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua litar adalah tepat, jadi yang kedua membelanjakan lebih banyak gate berbelit tanpa sebarang faedah. (Formula simetri tertib dua menggunakan kumpulan pertama dua kali pada separuh masa setiap satu, dan oleh itu kos bergantung pada kumpulan mana yang datang dahulu.) `filter` menerima predikat ke atas [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) dan membiarkan gate yang ditolak tidak disentuh, jadi satu pas boleh menaikkan tertib pada gate yang mendapat manfaat dan mengekalkan yang lain pada peringkat pertama. Predikat di bawah menerima gate hanya apabila operatornya memindahkan boson antara mod, iaitu apabila kumpulan gagal berkomutasi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you run the pass again, nothing changes: the factors it emits are *atomic*.\n"
msgstr "Jika anda menjalankan pas itu sekali lagi, tiada apa-apa yang berubah: faktor yang dikeluarkannya ialah *atomik*.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Atomic factors {#atomic-factors}"
msgstr "Faktor atomik {#atomic-factors}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") marked `atomic` has no definition, so [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") leaves it in place however often it is applied. A synthesis marks the factors it emits this way, and so does [`BosonicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-q-drift#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift\") for the terms it samples.\n"
msgstr "[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") yang ditandakan `atomic` tidak mempunyai takrifan, jadi [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") membiarkannya di tempatnya walau berapa kali ia digunakan. Sintesis menandakan faktor yang dikeluarkannya dengan cara ini, begitu juga [`BosonicQDrift`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-q-drift#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicQDrift\") untuk sebutan yang disampelnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is more than tidiness. Splitting a Hermitian group further, term by term, yields factors that are individually **not** Hermitian, and the exponential of a non-Hermitian operator is not unitary:\n"
msgstr "Ini lebih daripada sekadar kekemasan. Membahagikan kumpulan Hermitian dengan lebih lanjut, sebutan demi sebutan, menghasilkan faktor yang secara individu **tidak** Hermitian, dan eksponen operator bukan Hermitian tidak uniter:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Each factor must be Hermitian on its own. A Hermitian operator split into groups can produce non-Hermitian ones, such as a hopping term separated from its adjoint. Check with [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\"). An operator *without* groups is split term by term, and the qubit stage then rejects the factors with `Operator contains complex coefficients`. The symmetrization of an even order partially cancels the error of a non-Hermitian factor, so a wrongly grouped operator can look better at order 2 than at order 1 while still being wrong.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Awas\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Setiap faktor mesti Hermitian dengan sendirinya. Operator Hermitian yang dibahagikan kepada kumpulan boleh menghasilkan kumpulan bukan Hermitian, seperti sebutan lompatan yang dipisahkan daripada adjointnya. Semak dengan [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\"). Operator *tanpa* kumpulan dibahagikan sebutan demi sebutan, dan peringkat qubit kemudian menolak faktor dengan `Operator contains complex coefficients`. Simetrisasi tertib genap membatalkan sebahagian ralat faktor bukan Hermitian, jadi operator yang dikumpulkan dengan salah boleh kelihatan lebih baik pada tertib 2 berbanding tertib 1 sambil masih salah.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a short step {#repeat-a-short-step}"
msgstr "Ulang langkah pendek {#repeat-a-short-step}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a circuit-level alternative, build one short Trotter step and repeat it. [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") flattens the repetitions into one circuit and leaves the boundaries adjacent, so passes can act across them:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai alternatif peringkat litar, bina satu langkah Trotter pendek dan ulanginya. [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") meratakan ulangan menjadi satu litar dan membiarkan sempadan bersebelahan, supaya pas boleh bertindak merentasinya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass `insert_barriers=True` to keep the repetitions apart. A barrier is mapped onto every qubit of the registers it touches, because an encoding needs several qubits per mode and a mode has no per-qubit image of its own:\n"
msgstr "Hantar `insert_barriers=True` untuk mengekalkan ulangan terpisah. Penghalang dipetakan kepada setiap qubit bagi daftar yang disentuhnya, kerana pengekodan memerlukan beberapa qubit bagi setiap mod dan mod tidak mempunyai imej setiap qubit tersendiri:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `repeat` is unrelated to the `reps` of a synthesis method. A synthesis subdivides a *single* evolution into more, shorter factors. Repeating a circuit that holds one evolution merely multiplies its total time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  `repeat` tidak berkaitan dengan `reps` bagi kaedah sintesis. Sintesis membahagikan *satu* evolusi kepada lebih banyak faktor yang lebih pendek. Mengulang litar yang mengandungi satu evolusi hanya menggandakan jumlah masanya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combine with a qubit-level formula {#combine-with-a-qubit-level-formula}"
msgstr "Gabungkan dengan formula peringkat qubit {#combine-with-a-qubit-level-formula}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two levels compose, and where both approximate, the accuracy of the result is governed by the weaker of the two. Raising the bosonic order while the qubit-side formula stays first-order buys little. See `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` for the qubit-side formula. It keeps the Pauli term order that the mapper chose, and so `group_wise()` can emit the terms of each group adjacent to one another, and `simplify()` can pin a canonical order instead.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua peringkat boleh digabungkan, dan di mana kedua-duanya menganggar, ketepatan hasil ditentukan oleh yang lebih lemah antara keduanya. Menaikkan tertib boson sementara formula sebelah qubit kekal peringkat pertama memberikan sedikit manfaat. Lihat `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` untuk formula sebelah qubit. Ia mengekalkan tertib sebutan Pauli yang dipilih oleh pemeta, dan oleh itu `group_wise()` boleh mengeluarkan sebutan setiap kumpulan bersebelahan antara satu sama lain, dan `simplify()` boleh menetapkan tertib kanonik sebaliknya.\n"

